# What NOT to copy into the build context.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter most:
#   - .env* keeps real credentials out of the image. A COPY . . without this
#     bakes DATABASE_URL, the LinkedIn secret and the Razorpay keys into a
#     layer that anyone who can pull the image can read back.
#   - node_modules and .next are host artefacts built for Windows. Copying
#     them in would shadow the Linux ones npm ci installs, and sharp would
#     load a binary compiled for the wrong platform.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
.next
.gen-out
out
build

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Local scratch - root test-*.js are manual scripts, not part of the app
test-*.js
test-*.mjs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Docs that do not affect the build
*.md
!README.md
